WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:04.320
Welcome to Second Drink Performance Review.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.400
Oh, man, I found some fun new stuff for this one.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.680
I can't wait to hear, Angela.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.780
This episode is really great.

5
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.020
We have writer Larry Wilmar on with us to share about his time writing on The Office

6
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.060
and also playing Mr. Brown.

7
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:20.580
Yeah.

8
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:25.380
Larry was our very first writer from the show as a guest on our podcaSt.

9
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:25.900
I know.

10
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:26.520
I love that.

11
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.240
Well, Jenna, are you ready for some fun new tidbits?

12
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:29.680
Yes.

13
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.840
Performance Review has a fan favorite cold open.

14
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:39.240
It's when Dwight has decided to ditch having a desk chair, and instead he gets a fitness thingy.

15
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:39.940
Yeah.

16
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:40.240
Yeah.

17
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.080
The ball thing.

18
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.120
What do you call it?

19
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.320
The ball thing?

20
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.300
I mean, it's like a, what's that thing, a medicine ball?

21
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.720
But no, medicine balls are the small, heavy ones.

22
00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:50.280
They're heavy ones.

23
00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.520
I don't know what I call it.

24
00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.720
Well, I think the writers were trying to figure out what to call it as well because I found

25
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.120
candy bag alts for it.

26
00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:57.440
Oh.

27
00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.640
In the shooting draft, Jim had this little bit of extra dialogue.

28
00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.480
He would look at Dwight sitting on the ball thing, and then Dwight would look at him and

29
00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:05.660
say, do you know what this is?

30
00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.780
And Jim would say, it's a hippity hop.

31
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.480
The good ones have handles.

32
00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.360
And then they had a series of candy bag alts for what to call it.

33
00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.540
First, Dwight says, it's a fitness ball.

34
00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:16.600
It changed my life.

35
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.320
Fitness ball.

36
00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.700
I think that's what I would call it.

37
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.680
The next candy bag alt, Dwight says, it's a yoga orb.

38
00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:22.240
Oh.

39
00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.080
Now we're in the orb world.

40
00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:24.580
Okay.

41
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.100
The next one, Dwight says, it's a fitness orb.

42
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.820
Isn't that the one we settled on?

43
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.280
That's the one they settled on.

44
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.720
I did an internet search and could not find it being called an orb anywhere.

45
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:34.280
Oh.

46
00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.420
What was it called in your internet search?

47
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.020
Exercise ball, balance ball, stability ball.

48
00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:40.900
A lot of balls.

49
00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.200
A lot of balls, no orbs.

50
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.460
That's what she said.

51
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.440
I think our writer's room was having some fun there.

52
00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.440
Guess what else?

53
00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:46.780
What?

54
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.640
There was a DVD commentary for this episode.

55
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.200
That we never talked about?

56
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:51.740
Oh, no.

57
00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.080
It features Rainn Wilson, Oscar Nunez, Paul Lieberstein, Melora Hardin, Larry Wilmore,

58
00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:58.580
Paul Feig, and me.

59
00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.900
You were on a commentary and you didn't even mention it?

60
00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:03.960
No, I didn't.

61
00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:05.360
Oh, man.

62
00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.760
Well, it's got a ton of fun stuff, but I thought I'd share two things.

63
00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:09.300
Okay.

64
00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:14.420
First of all, when we interviewed Larry for this episode, he shared about the index cards

65
00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:15.660
on the writer's room wall.

66
00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.740
We talk about that in this breakdown.

67
00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:23.180
But I learned from the commentary that this episode was partly inspired by one of the

68
00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.220
cards on the wall.

69
00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.000
Here's what Larry had to say on the DVD commentary.

70
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:34.680
This is the start of the Thursday, Friday idea, which I remember that when this episode was

71
00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.780
put together, there were about four different ideas that were just scrunched together to make

72
00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:39.180
an episode.

73
00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.560
And Thursday, Friday was just on the board on a card.

74
00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:42.760
And I said, what's Thursday, Friday?

75
00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:43.560
Oh, yeah.

76
00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.000
That's when Dwight thinks it's Friday.

77
00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:46.440
But it's Thursday.

78
00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.940
I said, oh, that'd be great in this episode.

79
00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.760
So it just became part of this episode like that.

80
00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.340
It just seemed like a real funny thing to pull onto it.

81
00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:53.760
It is.

82
00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:54.360
I love that.

83
00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:54.920
I love that.

84
00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:57.200
Oh, Thursday, Friday.

85
00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:58.600
Just a card on the wall.

86
00:02:59.000 --> 00:02:59.880
Thursday, Friday.

87
00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:05.160
Larry also said there was a runner with Ryan where he purposely puts himself on a treasure

88
00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.560
hunt to escape the suggestion box meeting.

89
00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:08.060
Mm-hmm.

90
00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.560
It's in deleted scenes.

91
00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.340
It starts in the conference room.

92
00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:15.740
Michael takes a note from the suggestion box that says, look on the supply shelf.

93
00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.580
And then Michael asks Ryan to go and look.

94
00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.960
Then Ryan yells from outside the conference room in the bullpen, oh, hey, there's another

95
00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:23.240
note.

96
00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.680
It says, look on the windshield.

97
00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.800
Dwight says, which windshield?

98
00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.300
And Ryan says, it doesn't say, but I'll look on all of them.

99
00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.260
And he's basically, now he's out.

100
00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.300
He's in the parking lot.

101
00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.600
He's out of the office for the day.

102
00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.880
Do you think this was because they needed BJ in the writer's room?

103
00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:37.540
Probably.

104
00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:41.340
This was a construct to get him out of all of the background work.

105
00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:41.840
I bet.

106
00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:42.660
I think so.

107
00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:47.120
And then lastly, Jenna, you mentioned in our initial breakdown that there were some great

108
00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.620
deleted scenes for this episode.

109
00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.340
I remember there were so many.

110
00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.620
Almost 11 minutes of deleted scenes.

111
00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:58.480
And you know, in talking to Dave Rogers, we know a lot of these deleted scenes end up in

112
00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:01.720
the super fan episodes, but I think we need to hear a few of them.

113
00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.220
Great.

114
00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.420
First, Oscar has a talking head about why he is worried about his performance review.

115
00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:08.780
It's really funny.

116
00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:09.380
Let's hear it.

117
00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.320
Oscar, I'm ready for you.

118
00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.740
Today's performance review day, company-wide.

119
00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:20.080
And I'm a little concerned about my review.

120
00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.660
I exceeded my sick days and my personal days because I just couldn't take it.

121
00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.700
And I don't have a good answer for him when he asks me.

122
00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:31.260
Amazing.

123
00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:31.900
Amazing.

124
00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.020
He just couldn't take it.

125
00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:33.960
That's why he didn't come in.

126
00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:38.980
And so now he goes into the conference room to have his performance review, and he's prepared

127
00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.980
for Michael to have a reaction to the fact that he's missed so many days.

128
00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:45.200
And here's what Michael says.

129
00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.500
Michael says, so.

130
00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.860
And Oscar goes, Michael, I don't know what to say.

131
00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.760
And Michael goes, you're in accounting.

132
00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:54.460
Oscar says, yes.

133
00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:55.820
Yes, I am.

134
00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.420
I'm sorry about the extra days.

135
00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.780
I know it's past my limit.

136
00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:02.220
Michael says, so, good.

137
00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.680
Something to work on.

138
00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.240
Being here more.

139
00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:11.800
And then he looks around and says, I've always been a believer in people being here more.

140
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.140
Oscar looks at him for a beat, then looks to camera and subtly shrugs.

141
00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.420
I mean, does Oscar not know Michael?

142
00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:22.540
I don't.

143
00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:23.700
I wouldn't have worried.

144
00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.160
I don't think Michael's tracking anything outside of his own interests.

145
00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:27.700
I know.

146
00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:32.920
Next up in deleted scenes, Jim asks Michael about his date with Jan.

147
00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:33.640
Oh.

148
00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.280
Oh, in baseball terMs.

149
00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.340
And Jim is clearly messing with Michael.

150
00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:42.680
I went to the shooting draft and part of this is scripted, part of it is improvised.

151
00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:43.560
Let's hear it.

152
00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:44.820
That's.

153
00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.020
Uh-huh.

154
00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:46.600
That's great.

155
00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:47.500
Yes, it is.

156
00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:47.780
Yeah.

157
00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:48.560
Do you have fun?

158
00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:49.560
Yes, I did.

159
00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:52.780
Do you go to first base?

160
00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:55.440
Hell yeah.

161
00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:55.960
Oh yeah?

162
00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:56.320
Yeah.

163
00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:57.560
Do you go to second?

164
00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:58.520
What?

165
00:05:58.900 --> 00:05:59.220
Second?

166
00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:00.720
Kind of.

167
00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:01.000
Yeah.

168
00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:02.740
Over the shirt.

169
00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.120
My elbow.

170
00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:04.660
So.

171
00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:06.720
Okay, so close call in second.

172
00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.640
Was there an infield fly?

173
00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:11.320
Yep.

174
00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:11.940
Wait.

175
00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:12.560
Yes.

176
00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:13.320
Pop-up.

177
00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:15.720
No.

178
00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.800
Later there was.

179
00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:18.660
Really?

180
00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:19.240
Yes.

181
00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:22.320
So you got the signal from the third base coach.

182
00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:26.310
You know what I'm saying?

183
00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.850
Like if there was a, you know, fly out to deep right.

184
00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:29.290
Mm-hmm.

185
00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:30.030
You know.

186
00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:31.770
I'd run around second.

187
00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:32.910
He tagged up, didn't he?

188
00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:35.150
I didn't.

189
00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:36.610
You know, it was.

190
00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.730
It was dark, for one thing.

191
00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:48.390
In the shooting draft, this scene ends with Michael saying, you know, I, I'm more of a hockey person.

192
00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.170
Oh, I like that.

193
00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:50.650
Yeah.

194
00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:56.090
And then, lady, Michael makes a phone call that you will not believe.

195
00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:58.890
I don't even want to say more than that.

196
00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.350
You just have to hear who he calls.

197
00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:01.990
Okay.

198
00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.390
Yeah, that got a little out of control.

199
00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:06.930
Jan's taking a break, which is fine.

200
00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:07.870
I'm doing the same.

201
00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:08.990
Just chilling.

202
00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:11.410
Get my mind off of us.

203
00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:12.550
She's right.

204
00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.290
I need to be more professional at the office.

205
00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:16.750
When I'm at work, I need to focus on work.

206
00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:20.040
I should call her ex-husband.

207
00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:20.980
Hello.

208
00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:21.820
Is this Art Gould?

209
00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:23.600
Hi there.

210
00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:25.360
My name is Michael Scott.

211
00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:26.340
I work at Dunder Mifflin.

212
00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.620
I believe I work with your wife, ex-wife, Jan.

213
00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:30.460
Yeah, that's right.

214
00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:30.840
Yes.

215
00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:35.760
Um, I, uh, was wondering if I could ask a personal question about her.

216
00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:38.480
Mm-hmm.

217
00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.220
Okay, well, could I ask anyway?

218
00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:44.820
Uh-huh.

219
00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:47.620
Well, yeah, I'm just going to ask.

220
00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:53.480
When you guys were dating, was she sort of easy to get and then really hard to get?

221
00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.540
Yeah, that Gould is a real interesting guy.

222
00:07:57.960 --> 00:07:58.700
A gem.

223
00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:05.720
And it goes on, and Michael's like, well, if that phone call is any indication,

224
00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:08.160
the guy is not a nice guy.

225
00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:10.220
Like, any wonder it didn't work out.

226
00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:12.060
It is really funny.

227
00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.000
Oh, my gosh.

228
00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:16.740
All right.

229
00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:22.060
Finally, we need to wrap up this second drink with a Michael talking head from Deleted Scenes.

230
00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:26.160
I would describe it, but I don't want to ruin it.

231
00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:26.980
Another one.

232
00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:28.100
Yes, yes.

233
00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:32.280
What is an office?

234
00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:34.120
Is it a group of people?

235
00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:34.560
Maybe.

236
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.180
Is it an idea?

237
00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:37.240
Of course, yes.

238
00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:40.340
Is it a living organism?

239
00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:41.360
Exactly.

240
00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:42.180
Yes.

241
00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:46.900
And any single cell organism has to have a spine.

242
00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.100
And that's me.

243
00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:52.680
But the spine is always controlled by a brain.

244
00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.040
And that is Jan.

245
00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:56.460
But the brain needs a heart.

246
00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:57.520
And that is me again.

247
00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.020
So ironic.

248
00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:00.940
You know what?

249
00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:04.840
The heart is smarter than the brain.

250
00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:10.650
Brain is so effing hot.

251
00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:13.140
Okay.

252
00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:18.360
I am pretty certain I was there when he did that talking head because I am having, like,

253
00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:25.460
a flood of memories come in of being around the monitor watching that and loving it so very much.

254
00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.480
Oh, I'm so glad that exists somewhere now.

255
00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:29.260
Isn't that so great?

256
00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:29.600
Yes.

257
00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:31.560
But the brain is so effing hot.

258
00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:32.400
So effing hot.

259
00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.540
Well, that was my second drink.

260
00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.300
This is such a great episode.

261
00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.740
Thank you so much for those, Angela.

262
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.020
And now, everyone, here is our breakdown of performance review with Larry Wilmore.

263
00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:48.970
I'm Jenna Fisher.

264
00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.290
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

265
00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:51.550
We were on The Office together.

266
00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:52.810
And we're best friends.

267
00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:56.630
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

268
00:09:56.630 --> 00:10:01.010
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes

269
00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:03.630
stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

