1460
00:56:48.130 --> 00:56:49.010
That's all Rain.

1461
00:56:49.410 --> 00:56:51.150
And there was something funny about that.

1462
00:56:51.150 --> 00:56:56.690
So usually when you have music in a scene, they don't actually play the music on set.

1463
00:56:57.030 --> 00:57:00.810
In fact, there'll be like a big dance scene or a club scene.

1464
00:57:00.930 --> 00:57:02.150
Like, let's say you're shooting a wedding.

1465
00:57:02.390 --> 00:57:06.070
They'll play a few seconds of the music so that you can get the beat.

1466
00:57:06.150 --> 00:57:09.110
And then they turn it off and you have to dance.

1467
00:57:09.330 --> 00:57:10.190
With no music.

1468
00:57:10.290 --> 00:57:11.970
With no music and say your dialogue.

1469
00:57:12.250 --> 00:57:14.190
And then they add the music later in editing.

1470
00:57:14.370 --> 00:57:19.350
And that's so they can get your dialogue clean and so that they can cut between different takes.

1471
00:57:19.350 --> 00:57:21.630
And it, you don't want this song in the background.

1472
00:57:21.990 --> 00:57:27.810
Well, for this scene, they actually played the music on the boombox.

1473
00:57:28.030 --> 00:57:31.870
And it made for a bit of a challenge in the editing room.

1474
00:57:32.050 --> 00:57:38.490
But Greg felt like it provided so much to Rain's performance.

1475
00:57:38.490 --> 00:57:39.250
Performance, yeah.

1476
00:57:39.410 --> 00:57:41.930
For him to have that music blaring.

1477
00:57:42.310 --> 00:57:43.970
And also, it's documentary.

1478
00:57:43.970 --> 00:57:49.950
So you wouldn't have this, like, clean track of the music playing later.

1479
00:57:50.170 --> 00:57:51.970
Although we did in Cafe Disco.

1480
00:57:52.110 --> 00:57:53.510
We all had to dance to nothing.

1481
00:57:53.510 --> 00:57:53.930
